# CODEOWNERS — require maintainer review on the highest-risk surfaces.
#
# These are the paths where a careless or malicious change turns the repo into a
# supply-chain or privilege-escalation vector — the exact class of attack
# Blastgate itself models. Combined with branch protection's "Require review from
# Code Owners" rule, an outside contributor can still open a PR touching any of
# these, but it cannot merge without a maintainer's review.
#
# The GitHub owner of this repo is @jwolberg (per the git remote). Update these
# handles if maintainership changes.

# Catch-all: nothing ships un-owned.
*                       @jwolberg

# CI / workflows — the GITHUB_TOKEN permissions and untrusted-trigger surface.
/.github/               @jwolberg
/.gitlab/               @jwolberg

# The published GitHub Action entry point and its built bundle (dist/ is what
# runs when someone references this action — treat it like release infra).
/action.yml             @jwolberg
/dist/                  @jwolberg

# The engine and the OWASP taxonomy that findings are labeled against.
/src/                   @jwolberg
/package.json           @jwolberg
/package-lock.json      @jwolberg
